Requested via a coordinator feature-gap review, 2026-08-30. Extension repo:
../lsp-openplanet-ext/ (packages/vscode-ext). Enhancement.

## Gap
Verified on master: `contributes.commands` has exactly ONE entry,
`openplanetLsp.restart` ("Restart Server"). There are no `menus`, no
`keybindings`, and no status bar item. `activationEvents` is `[]`.

Consequences:
- There is no ambient signal the LSP is running, which server binary is in
  use, which type DB version is loaded, or which game target is active. When
  something looks wrong the user cannot tell whether the server is dead, stale,
  or simply disagrees with them.
- Server capabilities have no palette route (see B039 for the concrete case:
  `openplanet.regenerateTypeDb` is advertised and unreachable).
- Diagnosing a user report starts with "check the output channel", which
  requires knowing the output channel exists.

## Work

### Status bar item
Show a compact indicator: server state (starting / ready / failed), and on
hover a tooltip with the resolved server path, server version, type DB version
and source, active game target, and workspace root. Click opens the output
channel. Colour it as an error when the server has failed — that single
affordance replaces most of the "is it even running" support burden.

### Commands
Contribute, at minimum:
- `openplanetLsp.showLogs` — reveal the output channel. Trivial, and referenced
  by every other diagnostic path.
- `openplanetLsp.showStatus` — dump resolved config: server path/version, type
  DB version, game target, plugin roots, active defines, workspace roots.
  Prefer a read-only document over a notification; this is text people paste
  into bug reports.
- `openplanetLsp.regenerateTypeDb` — see B039, which owns the server-side
  verification. Contribute the palette entry here only if B039 lands first, or
  coordinate so it is not contributed twice.
- `openplanetLsp.restartVerbose` — restart with elevated server logging, for
  reproducing a report without editing settings.

### Wiring
- Set `activationEvents` explicitly (`onLanguage:angelscript` plus whatever the
  commands need) rather than relying on inference, so the status bar appears
  when it should and not on every window.
- Add `menus` entries where they help (editor context menu for the status dump
  is probably noise; the command palette is the main surface — do not add menu
  clutter without a reason).

## Design decision (coordinator, 2026-08-30)
`showStatus` output must be safe to paste in public. It names filesystem paths,
so it may include a home directory — abbreviate `$HOME` to `~` and do not
include environment variables wholesale. This is a bug-report aid; treat its
output as something that will end up in a GitHub issue.

The status bar must NOT poll the server. Drive it from the language client's
existing state-change events, plus the responses the extension already
receives. A per-second refresh for a mostly-static indicator is wasted work in
every open window.

## Test plan (vitest, the extension repo's existing harness)
Red:
- each new command is registered on activation and present in
  `contributes.commands` (registration and palette presence are separate
  failures — assert both)
- `showLogs` reveals the output channel
- `showStatus` produces a document containing the resolved server path,
  versions and game target
- the status bar item is created on activation and disposed on deactivate

Variants (per CLAUDE.md, generalize):
- server states starting / ready / failed / restarting each render a distinct
  status bar state, and the failed state is visually distinguished
- server never starts (bad `serverPath`) -> status bar shows failure and the
  tooltip names the reason; no unhandled rejection
- server crashes AFTER a successful start -> status bar updates rather than
  staying stale
- no workspace folder open -> commands still work or degrade with a clear
  message; no throw
- multi-root workspace -> status reflects the root for the ACTIVE editor, and
  switching editors updates it
- `showStatus` with `$HOME` in every path -> output contains `~`, not the
  literal home path
- deactivate with the server still starting -> clean disposal, no leaked
  listener
- commands invoked before activation completes -> queued or refused cleanly

